<usx version="3.1.2">
  <book code="ECC" style="id">EN_ULT en_English_ltr Thu Jul 07 2022 13:36:28 GMT-0500 (Central Daylight Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Ecclesiastes
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Ecclesiastes
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ecclesiastes
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Ecc
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Ecclesiastes

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="ECC 1"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 1:1"/>The words of Qoheleth, the son of David, king in Jerusalem,
<verse eid="ECC 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 1:2"/>“Vapor of vapors,” says Qoheleth.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:2">“Vapor of vapors; the whole {is} vapor.”

<verse eid="ECC 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 1:3"/>What profit {belongs} to humanity
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:3">in exchange for all his toil that he toils under the sun?

<verse eid="ECC 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 1:4"/>A generation is going and a generation is coming,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:4">but the earth is standing in perpetuity.
<verse eid="ECC 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 1:5"/>And the sun rises and the sun sets;
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:5">and to its place, panting, it is rising there.
<verse eid="ECC 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 1:6"/>Going to {the} south and turning to {the} north,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:6">turning, turning, the wind is going;
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:6">and on its courses, the wind is returning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 1:7"/>All the rivers are going to the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:7">but the sea—there is no fullness of it.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 1:7">To a place that the rivers are going—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:7">there, they are going again.
<verse eid="ECC 1:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 1:8"/>All the things {are} wearisome;
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:8">a person is not able to speak.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 1:8">An eye is not satisfied of seeing,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:8">and an ear is not filled from hearing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 1:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 1:9"/>Whatever that which was, it {is} that which will be,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:9">and whatever that which has been done, it {is} that which will be done.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:9">And there is not anything new under the sun.
<verse eid="ECC 1:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 1:10"/>{Is} there a thing about which one says,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:10">“See this, it {is} new?”
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 1:10">It already existed in ages
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:10">that were from before our faces.
<verse eid="ECC 1:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 1:11"/>There is not a memory of the former {times},
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:11">and also, of the latter {times} that will be;
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 1:11">memory will not be of them,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:11">along with those that will be at the latter {time}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 1:12"/>I, Qoheleth, was king over Israel in Jerusalem.
<verse eid="ECC 1:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 1:13"/>So I gave my heart to seek and to explore with wisdom concerning all that is done under the heavens. It {is} an unpleasant business God has given to the sons of humanity to be busy with it.
<verse eid="ECC 1:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 1:14"/>I saw all the deeds that are done under the sun, and—behold—everything {is} vapor and pursuit of wind.
<verse eid="ECC 1:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 1:15"/>A bent {thing}—one is not able to straighten {it},
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:15">and lack is not able to be counted.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 1:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 1:16"/>I spoke, I, with my heart, saying, “I—behold—I have grown and increased wisdom over all who were before my face over Jerusalem, and my heart has seen much wisdom and knowledge.”
<verse eid="ECC 1:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 1:17"/>So, I gave my heart to know wisdom and to know madness and folly. I know that also this—it {is} pursuit of wind.
<verse eid="ECC 1:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 1:18"/>For in much wisdom {is} much anger,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 1:18">and {when} one increases knowledge, he increases pain.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 1:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="ECC 2"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 2:1"/>I spoke, I with my heart, “Come, let me test you with joy and see good.” But behold, it also {was} vapor.
<verse eid="ECC 2:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 2:2"/>To laughter I said, “Madness!” And to joy, “What is this doing?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 2:3"/>I explored in my heart to drag my flesh with wine (and my heart was guiding {me} with wisdom) and to seize folly until I could see where {is the} good for the sons of humanity that they might do under the heavens {during} the number of the days of their lives.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 2:4"/>I enlarged my deeds. I built for myself houses. I planted for myself vineyards.
<verse eid="ECC 2:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 2:5"/>I made for myself orchards and royal parks, and I planted in them a tree of each fruit.
<verse eid="ECC 2:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 2:6"/>I made for myself pools of waters to cause to drink from them a forest of growing trees.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 2:7"/>I acquired male servants and female servants and sons of the house belonged to me. Also, much property of cattle and sheep belonged to me, more than all who were to my face in Jerusalem.
<verse eid="ECC 2:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 2:8"/>I also amassed for myself silver and gold and the treasure of kings and provinces. I appointed for myself male singers and female singers and the pleasures of the sons of humanity: breast and breasts.

<verse eid="ECC 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 2:9"/>So I became great, and I increased more than all who were to my face in Jerusalem. Also, my wisdom stood by me.
<verse eid="ECC 2:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 2:10"/>And all that my eyes asked, I did not refuse from them. I did not restrain my heart from any joy, because my heart {was} joyful from all my toil and this was my portion from all my toil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 2:11"/>And I turned, I, to all my works that my hands had done and to {the} toil that I toiled to do and behold, everything {was} vapor and pursuit of wind, and there was no profit under the sun.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 2:12"/>So I turned, I, to see wisdom and madness and folly, because what {can} the person {do} who will come after the king {than} that which he has already done?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 2:13"/>And I saw, I, that there is a profit for wisdom more than folly, as {there is} a profit of the light more than the darkness.
<verse eid="ECC 2:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 2:14"/>The wise, his eyes {are} in his head,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 2:14">but the fool in the darkness is walking.
</para>
  <para style="m" vid="ECC 2:14">But I know, even I, that one happening will happen to both of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:14"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 2:15"/>And I spoke, I, with my heart, “As {the} happening of the fool, even {to} me—it will happen {to} me! And why was I, I, wise then, abundantly?” And I said to my heart that also this {is} vapor.
<verse eid="ECC 2:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 2:16"/>For there is no memory of the wise {person} with the fool in perpetuity, because already, {in} the coming days, both {will be} forgotten. Alas! The wise die with the fool!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:16"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 2:17"/>And I hated life, because bad to me {was} the work that was done under the sun, because everything {was} vapor and pursuit of wind.
<verse eid="ECC 2:17"/><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 2:18"/>And I hated, I, all my toil that I had toiled under the sun, that I will leave it to the person who will be after me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ECC 2:19"/>And who knows: Will he be wise or a fool? And he will have authority over all my toil that I toiled and {for} which I was wise under the sun. Also, this {is} vapor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:19"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ECC 2:20"/>Then I turned, I, to cause my heart to despair concerning all the toil which I toiled under the sun.
<verse eid="ECC 2:20"/><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ECC 2:21"/>For there is a person whose toil {is} with wisdom and with knowledge and with skill, but to a person who has not toiled for it, he will give it {as} his portion. This also {is} vapor and a great misfortune.
<verse eid="ECC 2:21"/><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ECC 2:22"/>For what endures for the person in exchange for all his toil and in the striving of his heart {in} which he {is} a toiler under the sun?
<verse eid="ECC 2:22"/><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ECC 2:23"/>For all his days {are} pains, and anger {is} his business; even in the night, his heart does not rest. Also this—it {is} vapor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:23"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ECC 2:24"/>There is nothing better for humanity {than} that he should eat and drink and cause his spirit to see good in his toil. Also, this I saw, I, that it {is} from the hand of the God,
<verse eid="ECC 2:24"/><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ECC 2:25"/>for who will eat and who will enjoy apart from him?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 2:25"/><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ECC 2:26"/>For to a person who {is} good to his face, he gives wisdom and knowledge and joy. But to the sinner, he gives {the} business of gathering and of collecting to give to {the} one who is good to the face of the God. Even this {is} vapor and pursuit of wind.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 2:26"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="ECC 3"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 3:1"/>For everything {there is} a season, and a time for every matter under the heavens:
<verse eid="ECC 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 3:2"/>a time to give birth and a time to die,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:2">a time to plant and a time to tear out what was planted,
<verse eid="ECC 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 3:3"/>a time to kill and a time to heal,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:3">a time to break down and a time to build,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 3:4"/>a time to weep and a time to laugh,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:4">a time to mourn and a time to dance,
<verse eid="ECC 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 3:5"/>a time to throw stones and a time to gather stones,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:5">a time to embrace and a time to refrain from embracing,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 3:6"/>a time to seek and a time to lose,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:6">a time to keep and a time to throw away,
<verse eid="ECC 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 3:7"/>a time to tear and a time to mend,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:7">a time to be silent and a time to speak,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 3:8"/>a time to love and a time to hate,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 3:8">a time of war and a time of peace.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 3:9"/>What {is the} profit of the one who does in exchange for that which he {is} toiling?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 3:10"/>I saw the business that God gives to the sons of humanity to be busy with it.
<verse eid="ECC 3:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 3:11"/>He makes everything beautiful in its time. Also, he gives perpetuity in their heart, yet so that humanity cannot find the work that the God does from beginning to end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 3:12"/>I know that there is no good for them except to rejoice and to do good during his life,
<verse eid="ECC 3:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 3:13"/>and every person who eats and drinks and sees good in all of his toil—it {is} a gift of God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 3:14"/>I know that everything that God does, it will be enduring. To it, there is nothing to add, and from it, there is nothing to remove.
</para>
  <para style="m" vid="ECC 3:14">And God acts so that they fear from before his face.
<verse eid="ECC 3:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 3:15"/>Whatever that is, already it {was},
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 3:15">and that which is to be, already it is.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 3:15">And the God seeks that which is pursued.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 3:16"/>But again, I saw under the sun: The place of justice—there {was} wickedness, and the place of equity—there {was} wickedness!
<verse eid="ECC 3:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 3:17"/>I spoke, I with my heart: “The equitable and the wicked the God will judge, because a time {exists} for every matter and on account of every deed there.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:17"/><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 3:18"/>I spoke, I, with my heart, “For the sake of the sons of humanity, the God {is} to test them to see that {they are} animal{s}, they themselves.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ECC 3:19"/>For the happening of the sons of humanity and the happening of the animal—and one happening {is} for them. As the death of this {one}, so the death of this {one}, and one spirit {exists} for both. But an advantage of humanity over the animal, there is none, for everything {is} vapor.
<verse eid="ECC 3:19"/><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ECC 3:20"/>Both are going to one place. Both are from the dust, and both return to the dust.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:20"/><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ECC 3:21"/>Who knows? The spirit of the sons of humanity, it {is} the one going up, upwards, and the spirit of the animal, it {is} the one going down, downwards to the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 3:21"/><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ECC 3:22"/>So, I saw that there is nothing better than that humanity should rejoice in his works, for it {is} his portion. For who will bring him to look at what that will be after him?

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 3:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="ECC 4"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 4:1"/>And I turned, I, and I saw all the oppressions that were being done under the sun. And behold, the tears of the oppressed—and there was no comforter for them. And from the hand of {the ones} oppressing them {was} strength, and there was no comforter for them.
<verse eid="ECC 4:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 4:2"/>So I praised, I, the dead {people} who have already died more than the living, who, they are still alive.
<verse eid="ECC 4:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 4:3"/>But better than {the} two of them {is} the one who has not yet lived, who has not seen the evil deed that is being done under the sun.

<verse eid="ECC 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 4:4"/>And I saw, I, every toil and every success of the deed—that it {is} the envy of a person from his friend. This also {is} vapor and pursuit of wind.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 4:5"/>The fool is folding his hands
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:5">and is eating his flesh.
<verse eid="ECC 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 4:6"/>Better {is} a fullness of a palm {with} quiet
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:6">than a fullness of {two} handfuls {with} toil and pursuit of wind.

<verse eid="ECC 4:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 4:7"/>And I turned, I, and I saw a vapor under the sun:
<verse eid="ECC 4:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 4:8"/>There is one {person} and there is not a second {person}—even a son or brother, there is not for him—and there is no end to all his toil. Also, his eye is not satisfied {with} wealth. So why {am} I toiling and causing my soul to lack from good things? Even this {is} vapor, and it {is} an unpleasant business.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 4:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 4:9"/>Better {are} the two {people} than the one {person},
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:9">that there is for them a good wage in exchange for their toil.
<verse eid="ECC 4:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 4:10"/>For if they fall,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:10">the one {person} will lift up his companion,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 4:10">but woe {is} his—the one {person} that will fall,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:10">but there is no second {person} to lift him up.
<verse eid="ECC 4:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 4:11"/>Also, if two {people} lie down, then there is warmth for them.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:11">But for {the} one {person}—how will there be warmth?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 4:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 4:12"/>And if he will overpower him, the one {person},
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:12">the two {people} will stand against him,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 4:12">and the three-fold rope will not be torn in two quickly.

<verse eid="ECC 4:12"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 4:13"/>Better {is} a child, poor but wise, than a king, old but foolish, who does not know {how} to be warned any longer.
<verse eid="ECC 4:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 4:14"/>For from the house of those who are bound, he came forth to become king, yet even in his kingdom he was born poor.
<verse eid="ECC 4:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 4:15"/>I saw all the living, the ones walking around under the sun, with the second child who will stand under him.
<verse eid="ECC 4:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 4:16"/>There {was} no end to all the people, to all who were to their faces. Even the latter {people} will not rejoice in him, because even this {is} vapor and pursuit of wind.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 4:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="ECC 5"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 5:1"/>Keep your feet when you go to the house of God. And drawing near to listen {is better} than fools giving a sacrifice, for they are not knowing {that they} do evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 5:2"/>Do not be hurried concerning your mouth, and do not let your heart hurry to bring forth a word to the face of God. For the God {is} in heaven, but you {are} on the earth; therefore, let your words be few.
<verse eid="ECC 5:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 5:3"/>For the dream comes with much business,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:3">and the voice of a fool with many words.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 5:4"/>When you vow a vow to God, do not delay fulfilling it, for there is no delight in the fools. That which you vow, fulfill.
<verse eid="ECC 5:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 5:5"/>{It is} better that you do not vow than that you vow but do not fulfill.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 5:6"/>Do not give your mouth to cause your flesh to sin, and do not say to the face of the messenger that it {was} an unintentional sin. Why should God be angry concerning your voice and destroy the deed of your hands?
<verse eid="ECC 5:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 5:7"/>For in many dreams and vaporous things and many words—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:7">just fear God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 5:8"/>If {the} extortion of {the} poor and {the} robbery of justice and equity you see in the province, do not be amazed concerning the matter, for a high one over a high one is watching, and high ones {are} over them.
<verse eid="ECC 5:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 5:9"/>And a profit of a land—it {is taken} by all. {But} a king is served by a field.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 5:10"/>A lover of silver will not be satisfied {with} silver,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:10">and whoever loves increase, not income.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:10">Also this {is} vapor.
<verse eid="ECC 5:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 5:11"/>When the good {thing} increases,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:11">the {ones} eating it increase.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 5:11">And what advantage {belongs} to its master
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:11">except the sight of his eyes?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 5:12"/>Sweet is the sleep of the worker,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:12">however little or however much he eats,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 5:12">but the satisfaction of a rich person—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 5:12">it is not allowing him to sleep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:12"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 5:13"/>There is a sickening misfortune I have seen under the sun: Wealth kept by its master to his harm.
<verse eid="ECC 5:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 5:14"/>And that wealth perished in an unfortunate business. And he had fathered a son, but there was not in his hand anything.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 5:15"/>As he went out from the womb of his mother, naked he will go again, just as he came. And he will not take anything in exchange for his toil that he will take in his hand.

<verse eid="ECC 5:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 5:16"/>And also this {is} a sickening misfortune: Just as he came, thus he will go. And what profit {belongs} to him who toils for the wind?
<verse eid="ECC 5:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 5:17"/>Also, all his days in darkness he eats, and {in} great vexation and his sickness and anger.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:17"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 5:18"/>Behold what I, I, have seen {is} good: That {it is} beautiful to eat and to drink and to see good in all his toil that he will toil under the sun {during} the number of the days of his life that the God has given to him, for it {is} his portion.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 5:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ECC 5:19"/>Also, each person who the God gives to him wealth and possessions and has empowered him to eat from it and to accept his portion and to rejoice in his toiling—this, it {is} a gift of God.
<verse eid="ECC 5:19"/><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ECC 5:20"/>For not much does he remember the days of his life, because the God occupies {him} with the joys of his heart.


<verse eid="ECC 5:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="ECC 6"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 6:1"/>There is a misfortune that I have seen under the sun and it {is} great on humanity:
<verse eid="ECC 6:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 6:2"/>A person who the God gives to him wealth and possessions and honor, so he is not lacking for his soul from anything that he desires, but the God does not enable him to eat from it; instead, a nonnative person will eat it—this {is} vapor, and it {is} a sickening misfortune.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 6:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 6:3"/>If a man should father a hundred {children}, and many years should he live—and many that the days of his years may be—but {if} his soul is not satisfied from the good {thing} (and also a burial place is not for him), I say, “Better than him {is} the stillborn child.”
<verse eid="ECC 6:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 6:4"/>For in vapor, it came, and in the darkness, it will go, and in the darkness its name will be covered.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 6:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 6:5"/>Even {the} sun it did not see, nor did it know. {More} rest {belongs} to this one than this one.
<verse eid="ECC 6:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 6:6"/>And if he lived a thousand years twice, but a good {thing} he did not see—are not both going to one place?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 6:7"/>All the toil of humanity {is} for his mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 6:7">and yet the soul is not filled.

<verse eid="ECC 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 6:8"/>For what advantage {belongs} to the wise more than the fool? What {advantage belongs} to the poor person who knows {how} to walk before the living?
<verse eid="ECC 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 6:9"/>Better {is} a sight of {the} eyes
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 6:9">than the walking of {the} soul.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 6:9">Also this {is} vapor and pursuit of wind.

<verse eid="ECC 6:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 6:10"/>Whatever that is, already its name has been called, and it is known what a person {is}—and he is not able to contend with he who is more powerful than him.
<verse eid="ECC 6:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 6:11"/>When there are many words {that} are increasingly vaporous, what advantage {belongs} to humanity?
<verse eid="ECC 6:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 6:12"/>For who is knowing what {is} good for humanity in life {during} the number of the days of his vaporous life? And he makes them like the shadow. For who will declare to humanity what will be after him under the sun?

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 6:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="ECC 7"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 7:1"/>Better is a {good} name than good oil,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:1">and the day of death than the day of his being born.
<verse eid="ECC 7:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 7:2"/>Better to go to a house of mourning
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:2">than to go to a house of a banquet,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:2">because it {is} the end of all humanity
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:2">and the living will give {it} to his heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 7:3"/>Better grief than laughter,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:3">for with a bad face a heart may be well.
<verse eid="ECC 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 7:4"/>{The} heart of wise people {is} in a house of mourning,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:4">but {the} heart of fools {is} in a house of joy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 7:5"/>Better to listen to a rebuke of {a} wise {person}
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:5">than a person listening to a song of fools,
<verse eid="ECC 7:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 7:6"/>for like the sound of the thorns under the cooking pot,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:6">so {is} the laughter of the fool.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:6">And this also {is} vapor.

<verse eid="ECC 7:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 7:7"/>Surely oppression crazes {a} wise {person},
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:7">and a bribe destroys a heart.

<verse eid="ECC 7:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 7:8"/>Better {is the} end of a thing than its beginning.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:8">Better {is} length of spirit than height of spirit.
<verse eid="ECC 7:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 7:9"/>Do not hasten in your spirit to become angry,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:9">for anger rests in {the} lap of fools.

<verse eid="ECC 7:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 7:10"/>Do not say, “What was, that the former days were better than these?”
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:10">For you do not ask about this out of wisdom.

<verse eid="ECC 7:10"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 7:11"/>Wisdom is good with an inheritance
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:11">and an advantage to those who see the sun.
<verse eid="ECC 7:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 7:12"/>For {as} in the shadow of wisdom, {so} in the shadow of silver.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:12">And {this is} an advantage of knowledge: Wisdom preserves her owners.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:12"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 7:13"/>See the work of the God: For who is able to straighten that which he has bent?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 7:14"/>In a day of good, be in good,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:14">but in a day of misfortune, see—
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:14">indeed, the God has done this as well as this,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:14">so that humanity cannot find anything after him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:14"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 7:15"/>I have seen both in the days of my vapor:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:15">There is {a} righteous {person} perishing in his righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:15">and there is {a} wicked {person} lengthening in his evil.
<verse eid="ECC 7:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 7:16"/>Do not be overly righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:16">and do not be exceedingly wise—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:16">why should you be shocked?
<verse eid="ECC 7:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 7:17"/>Do not be very wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:17">and do not be a fool—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:17">why should you die when {it is} not your time?
<verse eid="ECC 7:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 7:18"/>{It is} good that you should take hold of this,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:18">and also from this, do not let your hand rest.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:18">For the {one who} fears God will go forth with both of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:18"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ECC 7:19"/>Wisdom is strong for the wise, more than ten rulers who are in the city.
<verse eid="ECC 7:19"/><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ECC 7:20"/>For a person—there is not a righteous {person} on the earth who does good and does not sin.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:20"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ECC 7:21"/>Also, to all of the words that they say, do not give your heart, so that you will not hear your servant belittling you.
<verse eid="ECC 7:21"/><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ECC 7:22"/>For even many times—your heart knows that even you have belittled others.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:22"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ECC 7:23"/>All of this I tested with wisdom. I said, “Let me be wise,” but it {was} far from me.
<verse eid="ECC 7:23"/><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ECC 7:24"/>Far away {is} that which was. And deep, deep—who can find it?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:24"/><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ECC 7:25"/>I turned, I, and my heart, to know and to explore and {to} seek wisdom and the scheme of things, and to know {the} wickedness {that is} folly and the foolishness {that is} madness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:25"/><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ECC 7:26"/>And I am finding more bitter than death:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:26">the woman who, she {is} snares—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:26">and nets, her heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:26">chains, her hands.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:26">{One who is} good to the face of the God will flee from her,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:26">but a sinner will be captured by her.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:26"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ECC 7:27"/>“See, this I have found,” says Qoheleth:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:27">One to one to find the scheme of things,
<verse eid="ECC 7:27"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ECC 7:28"/>while still my soul sought,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:28">but I have not found:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:28">One man from a thousand {men} I found,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:28">but a woman among all of these {people}, I did not find.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 7:28"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ECC 7:29"/>Only see this I have found:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 7:29">That the God made humanity upright,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 7:29">but they, they have sought out many schemes.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 7:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="ECC 8"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 8:1"/>Who {is} like the wise person,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:1">and who knows {the} interpretation of a matter?
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 8:1">{The} wisdom of a person enlightens his face,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:1">and the strength of his face is changed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:1"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 8:2"/>{As for} me—listen {to} the mouth of a king, that is, on account of the oath of God.
<verse eid="ECC 8:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 8:3"/>Do not be terrified from his face. Go! Do not stand in a bad matter, for everything that he pleases, he will do,
<verse eid="ECC 8:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 8:4"/>for {the} word of a king {is} authoritative. And who will say to him, “What are you doing?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 8:5"/>One who listens {to} a command will not know a bad matter,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:5">and {the} heart of a wise {person} will know {the} time and procedure,
<verse eid="ECC 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 8:6"/>because for every matter there is a time and procedure,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:6">because the misfortune of humanity {is} severe upon him,
<verse eid="ECC 8:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 8:7"/>for he is not knowing whatever that will be, for when it will be—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:7">who will declare {it} to him?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 8:8"/>There is no person authorized over the wind to restrain the wind,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:8">and there is no authority over the day of death,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 8:8">and there is no discharge in the war,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:8">and wickedness will not deliver its masters.

<verse eid="ECC 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 8:9"/>All this I saw {while} giving my heart to every deed that was done under the sun: A time that the person has authority over {another} person to his harm.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 8:10"/>And then I saw wicked people buried, and they entered, and from a place of holiness they went. And they were praised in the city where thus they had done. This also {is} vapor:
<verse eid="ECC 8:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 8:11"/>that a decree {against} the evil deed is not made quickly—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:11">therefore, the heart of the sons of humanity fills in them to do evil;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 8:12"/>that a sinner is doing evil a hundred times and lengthening {days} for himself—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:12">yet also I know that it will be good for those who fear God,
</para>
  <para style="q3" vid="ECC 8:12">who fear from before his face.
<verse eid="ECC 8:12"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 8:13"/>But it will not be good for the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q3" vid="ECC 8:13">nor will he lengthen {his} days like the shadow,
</para>
  <para style="q3" vid="ECC 8:13">because he is not fearing before the face of God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:13"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 8:14"/>There is vapor that is done on the earth:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 8:14">that there are righteous people
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:14">who {it} befalls to them like the deeds of the wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 8:14">and there are wicked people
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:14">who {it} befalls to them like the deeds of the righteous people.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 8:14">I say that also this {is} vapor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:14"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 8:15"/>And I praised, I, joy—that there is nothing good for humanity under the sun except to eat and to drink and to rejoice. And it will accompany him in his toil {during} the days of his life that the God has given to him under the sun.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 8:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 8:16"/>When I gave my heart to know wisdom and to see the business that is done on the earth—for even in the day and in the night sleep in his eyes he is not seeing—
<verse eid="ECC 8:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 8:17"/>then I saw every deed of the God: that humanity is not able to find the deed that is done under the sun, on account of which humanity toils to seek, yet he will not find, and even if the wise {one} says to know, he is not able to find.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 8:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="ECC 9"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 9:1"/>Indeed, all of this I gave to my heart to examine all of this: That the righteous and the wise and their work {are} in the hand of God. Either love or hate, humanity is not knowing; both {are} to their faces.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 9:2"/>Everything {is} as for everyone, one happening:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:2">for the righteous person and for the wicked person,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:2">for the good person and for the pure person and for the unclean person,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:2">and for the person who sacrifices and for the person who does not sacrifice.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:2">As the good person, so the sinner,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:2">the person who swears {an oath is} as the person who fears an oath.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 9:3"/>This {is} a misfortune about everything that is done under the sun: That one happening {belongs} to everyone. And also, the heart of the sons of humanity {is} full of evil, and madness {is} in their heart during their lives—and after him to the dead!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 9:4"/>For whoever that is joined to all the living,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:4">there is hope;
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:4">for a living dog—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:4">it {is} better than the dead lion,
<verse eid="ECC 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 9:5"/>for the living know that they will die,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:5">but the dead—they are not knowing anything,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:5">and there is no longer for them a reward—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:5">even their memory is forgotten!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 9:6"/>Even their love, even their hate,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:6">even their jealousy—already it has perished.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:6">And there is not for them a portion any longer in perpetuity
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:6">among all that is done under the sun.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 9:7"/>Go! Eat your bread with joy, and drink your wine with a good heart, because the God has already accepted your deeds.
<verse eid="ECC 9:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 9:8"/>At every time let your clothes be white, and do not let oil be lacking on your head.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 9:9"/>See life with {the} wife whom you love all the days of your vaporous life which he has given to you under the sun—all the days of your vapor. For it {is} your portion in life and in your toil that you {are} a toiler under the sun.
<verse eid="ECC 9:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 9:10"/>Everything that your hand finds to do, do {it} with your strength, because there is no deed or scheme of things or knowledge or wisdom in Sheol where you are going to there.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 9:11"/>I again saw under the sun:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:11">That not to the swift {is} the race,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:11">and not to the mighty {is} the war,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:11">and even not to wise {people is} bread,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:11">and even not to discerning {people is} wealth,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:11">and even not to understanding {people is} favor,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:11">for a time and the occurrence will happen to all of them.

<verse eid="ECC 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 9:12"/>For humanity does not even know his time.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:12">Like the fish that are caught in a troublesome net,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:12">and like the birds that are caught in the snare—
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 9:12">like them, the sons of humanity are snared at a time of misfortune
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:12">when it falls upon them suddenly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 9:13"/>Also, this I saw: Wisdom under the sun and great it {was} to me.
<verse eid="ECC 9:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 9:14"/>{There was} a small city, and a few men {were} in it. And against it came a great king, and he surrounded it, and he built against it great siegeworks.
<verse eid="ECC 9:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 9:15"/>And he found in it a poor wise man, and he himself delivered the city with his wisdom. But a person did not remember that poor man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 9:16"/>And I said, I, “Better {is} wisdom than might, but the wisdom of the poor person {is} despised, and his words—they are not heard.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 9:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 9:17"/>{The} words of wise people in quietness are heeded
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:17">more than the cry of a ruler among the fools.
<verse eid="ECC 9:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 9:18"/>Better {is} wisdom than weapons of battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 9:18">but one sinner will destroy much good.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 9:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="ECC 10"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 10:1"/>Flies of death cause a perfumer’s oil to putrefy {and} bubble;
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:1">weightier than wisdom or honor {is} a little foolishness.
<verse eid="ECC 10:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 10:2"/>{The} heart of a wise person, to his right,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:2">but a heart of a fool, to his left.
<verse eid="ECC 10:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 10:3"/>And even whenever the fool is walking on the road,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:3">his heart {is} lacking,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 10:3">and it says to everyone
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:3">{that} he {is} a fool.

<verse eid="ECC 10:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 10:4"/>If the spirit of the ruler rises against you, do not leave your place,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:4">for calmness will cause great sins to leave.

<verse eid="ECC 10:4"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 10:5"/>There is a misfortune I saw under the sun,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:5">like an unintentional sin that goes out from before the face of the authority.
<verse eid="ECC 10:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 10:6"/>Folly is placed into many high places,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:6">and rich {people} sit in the lowly place.
<verse eid="ECC 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 10:7"/>Indeed, I saw slaves on horses
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:7">and princes walking like slaves on the ground.

<verse eid="ECC 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 10:8"/>One who digs a pit will fall into it,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:8">and one who breaks through a wall—a snake will bite him.
<verse eid="ECC 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 10:9"/>Indeed, one who pulls up stones will be hurt by them;
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:9">one who splits wood will be endangered by them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 10:10"/>If the iron is dull,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:10">but he himself does not lighten the faces,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 10:10">he must exert strength.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:10">But a profit to succeeding {is} wisdom.
<verse eid="ECC 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 10:11"/>If the snake bites without a charm,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:11">then there is no profit for the master of the tongue.

<verse eid="ECC 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 10:12"/>{The} words of {the} mouth of a wise {person are} favor,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:12">but {the} lips of a fool will swallow him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 10:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 10:13"/>The beginning of the words of his mouth {is} foolishness,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:13">and {the} end of his mouth {is} evil insanity,
<verse eid="ECC 10:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 10:14"/>but the fool multiplies words.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:14">Humanity does not know what will be,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:14">and that which will be after him—who will declare {it} to him?

<verse eid="ECC 10:14"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ECC 10:15"/>The toil of foolish {people} wearies him,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:15">so that he does not know {how} to go to a city.

<verse eid="ECC 10:15"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ECC 10:16"/>Woe to you, land, that your king {is} a youth
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:16">and your princes eat in the morning.
<verse eid="ECC 10:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ECC 10:17"/>Blessed are you, land, that your king {is} a son of nobles
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:17">and {that} your princes will eat at the time with might and not with drunkenness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 10:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ECC 10:18"/>With laziness, the beams of the roof sink,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:18">and in idleness of hands, the house will leak.
<verse eid="ECC 10:18"/><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ECC 10:19"/>For laughter, {people} are making bread,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:19">and wine gladdens life,
</para>
  <para style="q3" vid="ECC 10:19">but silver answers everything.

<verse eid="ECC 10:19"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ECC 10:20"/>Even in your thought, do not belittle a king,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:20">and in the room of your bed, do not belittle a rich {person},
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 10:20">for a bird of the heavens will carry the voice,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 10:20">and a master of wings will declare {the} word.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 10:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="ECC 11"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 11:1"/>Throw your bread on the face of the waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:1">for in many days you will find it.
<verse eid="ECC 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 11:2"/>Give a portion to seven and even to eight,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:2">for you do not know what will be a misfortune on the earth.

<verse eid="ECC 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 11:3"/>If the clouds are filled with rain,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:3">they will pour out on the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 11:3">And whether a tree will fall in the south or in the north,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:3">{the} place where the tree will fall—there it will be.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 11:4"/>One who attends {to the} wind will not sow,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:4">and one who watches {the} clouds will not harvest.

<verse eid="ECC 11:4"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 11:5"/>Just as you are not knowing what {is} the way of the wind, as the bones {come} into the womb of the full {woman}, so thus you do not know the work of the God who does everything.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 11:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 11:6"/>In the morning sow your seed,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:6">and in the evening do not let your hand rest,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 11:6">for you are not knowing whether this one will prosper—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:6">this one or this one—
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:6">or whether two of them as one {will be} good.

<verse eid="ECC 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 11:7"/>And light {is} sweet,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:7">and {it is} good for the eyes to see the sun.
<verse eid="ECC 11:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 11:8"/>For if the man will live many years,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:8">in all of them let him rejoice,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 11:8">but let him remember the days of darkness
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:8">that they will be many.
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 11:8">Everything that is coming {is} vapor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 11:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 11:9"/>Rejoice young man in your youth and let your heart make you glad in the days of your young adulthood. And walk in the ways of your heart and in the sight of your eyes, but know that, on account of all these things, the God will bring you into judgment.
<verse eid="ECC 11:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 11:10"/>And remove anger from your heart and take misfortune away from your flesh, for youth and dark hair {are} vapor.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="ECC 11:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="ECC 12"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ECC 12:1"/>So, remember your Creator
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:1">in the days of your young adulthood,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 12:1">when the days of misfortune have not come
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:1">and the years arrive of which you will say,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:1">“There is not for me pleasure in them,”

<verse eid="ECC 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ECC 12:2"/>when the sun and the light
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:2">and the moon and the stars have not darkened
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:2">and the clouds return after the rain,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ECC 12:3"/>in the day when the guards of the house will tremble
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:3">and the men of valor will be bent over
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:3">and the women grinders cease because they are few
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:3">and those who look at the window will grow dark

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:3"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ECC 12:4"/>and {the} doors will be shut in the street,
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 12:4">when the sound of the grinding {is} low
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:4">and a person rises at the sound of the bird
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:4">and all the daughters of song are stooped;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ECC 12:5"/>also, they are afraid of a high {thing}
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:5">and terrors {are} in the way
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:5">and the almond tree blossoms
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:5">and the locust moves along
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:5">and the caper-fruit fails—
</para>
  <para style="q3" vid="ECC 12:5">for humanity is going to his eternal home
</para>
  <para style="q3" vid="ECC 12:5">and the mourners go around in the street—

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ECC 12:6"/>before the cord of silver is removed
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:6">and the bowl of gold is broken
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:6">and the pitcher is shattered at the fountain
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:6">and the wheel is crushed at the cistern
<verse eid="ECC 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ECC 12:7"/>and the dust returns to the earth as that it was
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:7">and the spirit returns to God who gave it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:7"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ECC 12:8"/>“Vapor of vapors!” says the Qoheleth. “Everything {is} vapor!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ECC 12:9"/>More {than} that Qoheleth was wise, again he taught the people knowledge, and he weighed and he searched. He ordered many proverbs.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ECC 12:10"/>Qoheleth sought to find words of pleasure, and words of truth were written rightly.

<verse eid="ECC 12:10"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ECC 12:11"/>{The} words of wise {people are} like goads, and like nails implanted {are} masters of collections. They are given by one Shepherd.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ECC 12:12"/>But more than them my son, be warned—of the making of many scrolls there is no end, and much study {is} weariness of flesh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="ECC 12:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ECC 12:13"/>The end of the matter,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:13">everything has been heard:
</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ECC 12:13">Fear God and keep his commandments,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:13">for this is the whole of humanity.
<verse eid="ECC 12:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ECC 12:14"/>For every deed the God will bring into judgment
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:14">concerning everything hidden,
</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ECC 12:14">whether good or whether evil.
<verse eid="ECC 12:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="ECC 12"/>
</usx>
